{"key":"enterprise/T1090.003","id":"T1090.003","name":"Multi-hop Proxy","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1090","tactics":["command-and-control"],"platforms":["ESXi","Linux","macOS","Network Devices","Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","network-infrastructure","onprem","virtualization"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may chain together multiple proxies to disguise the source of malicious traffic. Typically, a defender will be able to identify the last proxy traffic traversed before it enters their network; the defender may or may not be able to identify any previous proxies before the last-hop proxy. This technique makes identifying the original source of the malicious traffic even more difficult by requiring the defender to trace malicious…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1090/003","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--a782ebe2-daba-42c7-bc82-e8e9d923162d","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.706Z","source_object_version":"2.4","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0004","name":"Firmware Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0004","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--b9d031bb-d150-4fc6-8025-688201bf3ffd","page":"telemetry/DC0004/"},{"id":"DC0082","name":"Network Connection Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0082","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--181a9f8c-c780-4f1f-91a8-edb770e904ba","page":"telemetry/DC0082/"},{"id":"DC0085","name":"Network Traffic Content","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0085","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3772e279-27d6-477a-9fe3-c6beb363594c","page":"telemetry/DC0085/"},{"id":"DC0078","name":"Network Traffic Flow","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0078","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--a7f22107-02e5-4982-9067-6625d4a1765a","page":"telemetry/DC0078/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0359","name":"Multi-hop Proxy Behavior via Relay Node Chaining, Onion Routing, and Network Tunneling","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0359","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--407286ed-c904-412a-9f2d-7426ea7304a4","relationship_id":"relationship--393a41c9-3c31-4325-9af0-c7601db3cc77"}],"analytics":[{"id":"AN1020","name":"Analytic 1020","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0359#AN1020","guidance":"Suspicious processes (e.g., Tor clients, relays, unknown binaries) launch with sustained encrypted outbound traffic to known anonymity infrastructure (e.g., Tor, I2P), and may relay to additional internal systems via reverse proxying, ICMP tunneling, or socket forwarding.","platforms":["Windows"],"strategy_id":"DET0359"},{"id":"AN1021","name":"Analytic 1021","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0359#AN1021","guidance":"Tools such as `tor`, `nglite`, `proxychains`, `chisel`, or custom daemons repeatedly initiate outbound sessions to multiple nodes before final destination. This behavior is abnormal for Linux services outside of VPN, monitoring, or CDN relay contexts.","platforms":["Linux"],"strategy_id":"DET0359"},{"id":"AN1022","name":"Analytic 1022","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0359#AN1022","guidance":"LaunchAgents or LaunchDaemons initiate persistent Tor or relay processes that make encrypted outbound connections. May be paired with sandbox bypasses or unsigned executables communicating over SOCKS proxies.","platforms":["macOS"],"strategy_id":"DET0359"},{"id":"AN1023","name":"Analytic 1023","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0359#AN1023","guidance":"Outbound encrypted traffic initiated from hypervisor shell or via VM backdoor mechanisms to relays in VPS infrastructure, especially if traversing multiple nodes before reaching Internet destination. Packet captures or firewall logs show non-VM communication paths.","platforms":["ESXi"],"strategy_id":"DET0359"},{"id":"AN1024","name":"Analytic 1024","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0359#AN1024","guidance":"Encrypted traffic or ICMP tunneling from border routers to internal routers or unknown external IPs. Forwarded traffic shows consistent hop-to-hop relaying without matching configured VPN or expected network topology.","platforms":["Network Devices"],"strategy_id":"DET0359"}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0082","component":"Network Connection Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=3, 22","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN1020","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0359#AN1020","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0082/"},{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=1","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN1020","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0359#AN1020","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"component_id":"DC0078","component":"Network Traffic Flow","name":"dns:query","channel":"Outbound resolution to hidden service domains (e.g., `.onion`)","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN1020","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0359#AN1020","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0078/"},{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"auditd:SYSCALL","channel":"execve for proxy tools","platforms":["Linux"],"analytic_id":"AN1021","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0359#AN1021","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"component_id":"DC0078","component":"Network Traffic Flow","name":"NSM:Flow","channel":"conn.l